@title Boot to live gameplay, no driving input
@game  PCSA00027

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS IS: the shortest input timeline that leaves the title sitting in
# LIVE GAMEPLAY with nothing held. It exists to be a PREFIX, not a playthrough:
#
#   session --game <app> --dir <sess> --recipe .../gameplay-prefix.recipe --to 1800
#   explore --game <app> --recipe .../gameplay-prefix.recipe --at 1800 ...
#
# Both of those apply their own input from the frame they stop at, so the prefix
# must not still be holding anything (or scheduling a press later on) when they
# take over - a segment further down the timeline would silently override the
# experiment's input the moment the run passed its frame. That is why the drive
# inputs live in tutorial-drive.recipe and NOT here: this file ends at f1562.
#
# THE FRAME NUMBERS ARE ON THE CORRECTED CLOCK (a frame is a display-queue flip
# and nothing else). Anything recorded before 2026-07-25 counted voluntary
# yields too and ran about 80x fast, so old landmark frames do not apply.
#
# EVERY PRESS IS HELD 12 FRAMES ON PURPOSE. The guest samples the pad exactly
# once per display frame, so a 1-2 frame press can fall between two samples and
# is then never observed at all - which looks exactly like a title that ignores
# input. If a press here ever stops working, check whether the guest polled
# (RUST_LOG=vitaslop::input=trace) before retiming it.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# Legal splash to ~f450, then a "Communicating with server" spinner to ~f600.
# No input is accepted or needed through either.

800: @section accept-terms
# The ONLINE TERMS dialog is live and scrolling by f800; Cross accepts it.
820: cross
832:

1250: @section dialogs
# Three dialogs walk the tutorial intro. The exact frames are not critical (each
# dialog waits indefinitely), but they must be far enough apart that the next
# dialog has appeared before the next press lands.
1250: cross          # "Welcome to the ... tutorial"
1262:
1400: cross          # "There are 2 control schemes available..."
1412:
1550: cross
1562:

# By f1800 the tutorial shows its driving instruction with the REGULAR CONTROLS
# legend up (left stick = rotate in direction, L = accelerate, R = brake), and
# the car is under player control. Nothing is held from here on.
1800: @note live gameplay reached with a neutral pad - drive from here
